==Old English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|ang|heafoc}}, {{l|ang|heafuc}} (''Mercian''), {{l|ang|hafuc}}

===Etymology===
From an early form ''hæbuc'', from {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*habukaz}}, possibly from a {{inh|ang|ine-pro|*kobuǵos}}, perhaps ultimately derived from {{m|ine-pro|*keh₂p-||seize}}. Cognate with {{cog|ofs|havek}} ({{cog|fy|hauk}}), {{cog|osx|havuk}} ({{cog|nds|Haavk}}), {{cog|nl|havik}}, {{cog|goh|habuch}}, {{m|goh|habuh}} ({{cog|de|Habicht}}), {{cog|non|haukr}} ({{cog|sv|hök}}, {{cog|da|høg}}, {{cog|no|hauk}}, {{cog|is|haukur}}). The word is related to a Slavic word for a bird of prey ({{cog|ru|кобец}}, {{cog|pl|kobuz}}). Compare also {{cog|la|capys}}, {{m|la|capus||bird of prey}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈhɑvok/|lang=ang}}

